[h2]0.6.0[/h2]
[h3]Technical School[/h3]
[list]
[*]Beavers now study in their free time, with no staff. Every adult tries to get educated, and a beaver can learn every profession.
[*]Each school teaches one profession; pick it with the Teach buttons. Graduation takes 16 study hours for Metallurgy, 24 for Flight and 32 for Nuclear.
[*]Each profession uses its own supplies: Metal Block, Deep Alloy and Corn Ration for Metallurgy; Electronics, Yellowcake and Medicine for Nuclear; Electronics, Recovered Telemetry and Packaged Food for Flight.
[*]The school seats 12 students. Selecting a school with students inside no longer crashes the game.
[/list]
[h3]Balance[/h3]
[list]
[*]Late-game science climbs to the reactor: Mission Control 30,000, Rocket Assembly Hangar 50,000, Launch Pad 80,000, uranium and sludge buildings 200,000, Waste Refinery 500,000, reactor 1,000,000.
[*]The Nuclear Reactor now makes 800,000 hp.
[*]The Smog Scrubber now cleans all smog within 20 tiles.
[/list]
[h3]Other changes[/h3]
[list]
[*]Storage holding radioactive waste, sludge or contaminated water can no longer be deleted until it is emptied.
[*]Deep Frontier buildings are grouped into nine toolbar sub-groups.
[*]43 building models are much lighter (about 30% fewer triangles overall), so the game uses less memory, loads faster and shows placement previews more smoothly.
[*]Splitting a large power network no longer freezes the game.
[/list]
